target: internal/report/report.go
verify: go test ./internal/report/ -count=1 -run 'TestParityWithPrReport'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    an empty container is FALSY in Python, so `[] or ""` and `{} or ""` are both "", and the report renders nothing. This is a PRESENCE divergence rather than the punctuation one the enumerated list already covers for non-empty containers: measured against the oracle, `"findings": []` renders "ok,  finding(s)" there and "ok, [] finding(s)" here, and `"status": {}` the same. The function immediately below tests falsiness by VALUE rather than by spelling for numbers; the container cases were left matched by spelling, which is the same defect one type over — and matched by spelling they were bypassable, since a json.RawMessage keeps the writer's internal whitespace. The switch now runs on json.Compact's output, so `[ ]` and `{\t}` reach it as `[]` and `{}`.
--- old
	case "false", "null", `""`, "[]", "{}":
--- new
	case "false", "null", `""`:
